# promise: #466
# A right-click on a page opens Chromium's page menu (Arc's items) on screen. 0.1.44, the first
# release on Cra's own engine, built the menu and then showed nothing: Chrome only draws it in a
# views window, and Cra's pages sit in Cra's windows (engine patch context-menu-embedded-view).
# The menu's rows are read as it opens, then it closes.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=page
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://debug?menuShown=next
expect-log Cra menu shown: waiting
cra://debug?cdp=Input.dispatchMouseEvent&params={"type":"mousePressed","x":300,"y":300,"button":"right","buttons":2,"clickCount":1}
cra://debug?cdp=Input.dispatchMouseEvent&params={"type":"mouseReleased","x":300,"y":300,"button":"right","buttons":0,"clickCount":1}
expect-log Cra menu shown: Back\|.*Reload\|.*View Page Source\|Inspect$
